<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees Feb CPI at 0.1 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its February consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     2.2  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.4   (0.3)     2.3  (3.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     3.4  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.2   (0.6)     3.1  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.8   (0.0)     2.8  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (1.6)     2.5  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.9  (-0.6)     3.3  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.0  (-0.3)    -0.2  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     5.1  (6.2)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.9   (0.0)     3.1  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.0)    -0.9 (-0.8)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
